   "since": "2026-09-21",
   "unit": null,
   "value": "The Government Printing Office was created by Congress in June of 1860 as an agency of the legislative branch of the Federal Government. GPO is the Federal Government's primary centralized resource for gathering, cataloging, producing, providing, authenticating, and preserving published information in all its forms. GPO is also responsible for the production and distribution of information products and services for all three branches of the Federal Government.\r\n\r\nIn December 2014 legislation was passed that changed the agency's name from Government Printing Office to Government Publishing Office. \r\n\r\n",
